+`runtime.prepare_voice(...)` forwards clean mono float32 reference samples at their original sample rate by default; ONNXVoice owns Sopro reference preprocessing. Explicit `resampler="linear"` or `resampler="audiosig"` selects a legacy SoproSynth-side conversion override. Reuse a `PreparedVoice` only with its creating runtime; its state is not portable across runtimes, model revisions, or processes. `runtime.measure_request(request)` uses ONNXVoice text preparation to report the exact model-token count and authoritative `fits` result for the exact public request. With no external maximum, a request the runtime can execute under its automatic boundary policy returns `fits=True` even when `maximum=None`; the missing finite maximum does not mean fit is unknown. The optional `maximum` is a caller-supplied token limit. `max_segment_chars` controls internal character segmentation and is not a model-token maximum.

 `request_api_contract().supports_streaming` and `runtime.capabilities.supports_streaming` are both `False` until the opt-in released-wheel real-model integration gate passes. The synchronous `stream()` and `stream_text()` APIs are implemented, but streaming is not yet advertised as a supported capability. The request contract reports automatic text boundaries (`caller_owns_text_boundaries=False`) and support for the native/raw output policy.

